 pve-qemu-kvm (11.1.3-2) trixie; urgency=medium
 
   * vma: speed up restores by merging contiguous writes into one request and
     by avoiding an extra copy of each write when the page cache is bypassed,
     as for restores to ZFS pools. For example, restoring an 8 GiB disk to a
     ZFS volume on NVMe took about half the time.
 
   * vma: name the disk and the reason when a write or flush fails on restore,
     for example "blk_pwrite to drive-scsi0 failed - No space left on device",
     instead of only showing a negative error number.
